        "description": "<img src='https://i.cbc.ca/ais/9568d5b3-0a06-4b6c-9d7e-097c872d6a68,1777592981485/full/max/0/default.jpg?im=Crop%2Crect%3D%280%2C0%2C6000%2C3375%29%3BResize%3D%28620%29' alt='Three plumes of smoke tailings are seen stretching across the horizon.' width='620' height='349' title='Rocket practice rounds are launched from M142 High Mobility Artillery Rocket System (HIMARS) during a testing drill in Pingtung County, Southern Taiwan, Monday, May 12, 2025.'/><p>A U.S. contract notice shows Canada is included in a $1.1-billion High Mobility Artillery Rocket Systems (HIMARS) production deal, suggesting Ottawa finalized the purchase months ago without making any announcement. The silence clashes with promises to buy less American equipment, even as the Armed Forces pushes for the Ukraine-tested system to fill a critical long-range strike gap.</p>",
